    b: "Adenomas genuinely are considered the probable precursor of most colorectal cancers, so this true statement is not the exception.",
    c: "Only a minority of individual colonic adenomas ever progress to cancer, even though adenomas collectively are the precursor of most colorectal cancers — these are two different claims, and the statement that 'most adenomas progress to cancer' overstates any individual polyp's risk. The likelihood of a given adenoma progressing rises with its size, villous architecture and degree of dysplasia, not simply with the passage of time. This distinction between the population-level statement and the individual-polyp-level statement is exactly what the question is testing.",
